<speak>A short note of things to attend to afterwards can be easier than taking the documents themselves. It also gives you a clean stopping point before you leave. Perhaps your Sunday diary routine could include a quick check that the personal paperwork is where you expect it to be, rather than adding a separate evening of filing. I would not want to make your household routine more complicated. For our ordinary contact, we can keep the distinction simple: scheduled calls at agreed times, routine correspondence through your preferred channel, and administrative assistance separately when you need it. That is usually easier to maintain than several overlapping arrangements.</speak>